  "body": "Positioned in a peaceful setting, just an easy walk from Okoromai Bay and the coastal tracks of Shakespear Park, this well-designed two-storey home offers a combination of space, privacy and practical modern living.\r\n\r\nThe home welcomes you through a spacious entrance foyer, with high ceilings and generous glazing creating a light-filled first impression. Upstairs, durable bamboo flooring flows through the open-plan living and dining area, where large windows take full advantage of the elevated views across Okoromai Bay. Whether entertaining guests or enjoying a quiet evening at home, this space provides a comfortable setting with the changing coastal outlook as its backdrop.\r\n\r\nThe contemporary kitchen is well equipped for everyday use and entertaining, with streamlined cabinetry, generous bench space and a substantial walk-in scullery providing additional preparation and pantry storage. Also positioned on this level is the master bedroom, along with a separate single bedroom offering flexibility as a nursery, dressing room or dedicated home office.\r\n\r\nDownstairs, two generous double bedrooms create a separate accommodation zone, ideal for teenagers, extended family or visiting guests wanting their own space. The lower level offers a sense of privacy and separation from the main living areas, with one of the bedrooms opening directly onto a sheltered patio. Surrounded by established trees and mature foliage, this outdoor area provides a private spot for morning coffee, outdoor dining or simply relaxing.\r\n\r\nThe practical features are equally impressive. A double internal-access garage provides secure parking along with additional space for workshop activities and storage. Outside, extensive off-street parking caters for multiple vehicles, with plenty of room for a boat, tractor or motorhome. The integrated rooftop solar system is another valuable addition, helping improve energy efficiency and reduce ongoing household electricity costs.\r\n\r\nWith its flexible floor plan, elevated ocean views, generous parking and proximity to the coast and regional park, this property offers an appealing option for families, those needing additional accommodation or buyers looking to enjoy a relaxed coastal lifestyle.\r\n\r\nDeadline Sale 4.00pm Wednesday 2 December at Ray White Manly offices (unless sold prior).",
